{"id": "EUVD-2026-82226", "enisaUuid": "05d718ac-ebf6-3cfc-9e36-249eaf05622f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: aspeed_udc: check endpoint DMA allocation\n\nast_udc_probe() allocates a coherent DMA buffer used as the backing store\nfor endpoint buffers. ast_udc_init_ep() derives per-endpoint buffer\npointers from udc->ep0_buf, so a failed allocation is dereferenced during\nprobe.\n\nCheck the allocation before endpoint setup. The existing probe error path\ncalled ast_udc_remove(), which unregisters the gadget unconditionally and\nis not safe before usb_add_gadget_udc() succeeds. Add a local cleanup\nhelper for probe failures so pre-registration failures only unwind the\nresources that were actually initialized.\n\nThis was found by a local static analysis checker for unchecked allocator\nreturns while scanning Linux 6.16. The change was checked by applying it\nto current mainline and by running checkpatch. I do not have access to\nAspeed UDC hardware, so no runtime testing was performed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7ae1a48e70e9c3451b7dc7bc3896c82884bc4df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aaad88f857498ed1294f061f0b25d27ae891c55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6182e708e2e1f55521c8a01d7535630ecc2d7df9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff6e88e29965bd06f640e59acdcf0bbf04a7f55c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e6f57107c1886052d4baaa047a2bc3d0e91be5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97cee53a94be3bd4fd8fbed6071bd2f32dad1ab1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93118", "GHSA-m596-7j6r-7chf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15f1fa62-1b01-3110-b5d7-7318055ac403", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "055276c1320564b0192b3af323b8cc67f9b665e1 <9e6f57107c1886052d4baaa047a2bc3d0e91be5d"}, {"id": "16ca27a8-0abc-3378-b353-0667097a1e2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "2215f055-1e6b-3473-958b-26cec37038ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "055276c1320564b0192b3af323b8cc67f9b665e1 <97cee53a94be3bd4fd8fbed6071bd2f32dad1ab1"}, {"id": "222792f5-2e48-34f2-a218-90b33f6ee705", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "2378d34e-1633-3a84-a28e-f7e85fe9d9f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "3f2cdc5e-40cf-3849-8ac4-c955df0c85c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "434ec252-c2a6-3cfa-b4d6-402752a60de1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "055276c1320564b0192b3af323b8cc67f9b665e1 <4aaad88f857498ed1294f061f0b25d27ae891c55"}, {"id": "6f23cdd5-eca3-3eaf-9f61-e75beed1b131", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a22fbe2c-44ec-35c4-9e70-4178239849e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a83a7a35-d95b-3156-bca8-cb1bd1d80500", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "055276c1320564b0192b3af323b8cc67f9b665e1 <6182e708e2e1f55521c8a01d7535630ecc2d7df9"}, {"id": "d53c2442-dd0d-3215-b8ce-1d76729699df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "ddf892a7-4c7e-3950-aace-91a2f9f62a49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "f38f74e8-89e9-39ce-9090-7402fe9e02fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "055276c1320564b0192b3af323b8cc67f9b665e1 <ff6e88e29965bd06f640e59acdcf0bbf04a7f55c"}, {"id": "fa81bdab-c654-3419-bb64-aefdaf37fd4b", "product": {"na